{"authored" [{"question" "q-15174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x={t}^{3}+{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{3}-{t}^{2}$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+{t}^{2})=3{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})=3{t}^{2}-2t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{(3{t}^{2}+2t)}^{2}+{(3{t}^{2}-2t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+12{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}-12{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{18{t}^{4}+8{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{3{t}^{2}+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+2t+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+24t+8}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=t-1,\\,y={t}^{2}+2$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=2$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2)=2t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{{(1)}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4t+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{4+4t+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{4+t+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{t+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t),\\,y=t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}+(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+1+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+1+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21354" "fiel