{"question" "q-21354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21354" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-1,\\,y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+2$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-1) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+2) \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{36{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+2{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{6{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)-2{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-21339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡(3t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/8868658c9bc7195f435a0109fce26b8a4fa39324c0a9a39e3fb644c5f02cdc9b.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t),\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown above)?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t))=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))^{2}+(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{25{sin}^{2}⁡(5t)+36{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "76f1416cb6770f11d9b437e963585d4132b9f73be015e972b94b9a278e54e487" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{5{sin}^{2}⁡(5t)+6{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{10{sin}^{2}⁡(5t)+12{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{25\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+36\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{25\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+36{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-123030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{25{sin}^{2}⁡(5t)+36{cos}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/state.json" "file_sha256" "66ce47ef76cc642f29ab7ba3cb3c0119565533d581199c3bcb7f32d191f6520f" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/834eff403ac2a6f696e104ec914cac1b951f8a6d989e11c0e9f2576ac9e7f0d8.png)\n\nFind an integral expression for the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-t, \\quad y= \\dfrac{2}{3} t^{3/2}, \\qquad t\\in[0,1].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-602.json" "file_sha256" "1f357f0ff72d7e19f94ea030095cc693c81863dbdaa0c179e931b9bd339205f9" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} \\sqrt{ \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2 + \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\:\\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2})={t}^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{(-1)}^{2}+{({t}^{1/2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-602.json" "file_sha256" "1f357f0ff72d7e19f94ea030095cc693c81863dbdaa0c179e931b9bd339205f9" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the expression that gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=t, \\, y=\\ln{(\\cos{t})}$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ (see graph below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/48de26c11ae08afb45ec19ee56e770f7418f9be2afb8ee7dd46a0d1136cb125b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-7130.json" "file_sha256" "4b95462ac1beffe8f0371d72dcd570adcc4453d9a18adb64c59c806e57e25794" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL = \\int_{t_1}^{t_2} \\sqrt{ \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2 + \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}t}\\right)^2}\\:\\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t))=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(1)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+{tan}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{sec}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-7130.json" "file_sha256" "4b95462ac1beffe8f0371d72dcd570adcc4453d9a18adb64c59c806e57e25794" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=e^t(\\cos{t}+\\sin{t}), \\quad y=e^t(\\cos{t}-\\sin{t}) , \\quad t\\in \\left[0,\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right].\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/assets/15d185178bf8882f837c19361d630c0e537e145ca2337cad4655677255d0348a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-603.json" "file_sha256" "0b1465a151789c1895ad8501865c5beb11207ea792c1f50fd326b697b35d37a8" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-603" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+{e}^{t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+{e}^{t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{(2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2t}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{e}^{t}{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2({e}^{\\pi /4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/example-603.json" "file_sha256" "0b1465a151789c1895ad8501865c5beb11207ea792c1f50fd326b697b35d37a8" "basis" 1149 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010979/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-15174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x={t}^{3}+{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{3}-{t}^{2}$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+{t}^{2})=3{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})=3{t}^{2}-2t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{(3{t}^{2}+2t)}^{2}+{(3{t}^{2}-2t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+12{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}-12{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{18{t}^{4}+8{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fca83d133dfbce94c6d6fb8122c09b1e7028fadefab673818953b0808b76345f"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{3{t}^{2}+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+2t+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+24t+8}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-15174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{18{t}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-123025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=3{t}^{3}+5,\\,y={t}^{2}-5t$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=2$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-123025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{3}+5)=9{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-5t)=2t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{(9{t}^{2})^{2}+(2t-5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{81{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-20t+25}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-123025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fca83d133dfbce94c6d6fb8122c09b1e7028fadefab673818953b0808b76345f"} {"question" "q-123025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-123025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+{t}^{2}-5t+6}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "3{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{27{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-t+6}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{81{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-20t+25}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{85{t}^{4}-20t+25}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-20t+5}