n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}+(2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+4}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-123020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fca83d133dfbce94c6d6fb8122c09b1e7028fadefab673818953b0808b76345f"} {"question" "q-123020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-123020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{3{t}^{4}+1}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+3}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2}\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+t}\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-123020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+4}\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-123019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/assets/0a58808ee9b20e201d1ea8a31683f742e02f739127640de2fea87ce4757e7901.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=3{t}^{2},\\,y=5t$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$ (shown above)?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-123019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})=6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t)=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{(6t)^{2}+(5)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{36{t}^{2}+25}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/