{2}+2$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=2$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2)=2t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{{(1)}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/state.json" "file_sha256" "2e0226043fed6ba0104c5d1ce045f228d357296f9c74a07382d19d96cfe7c2e5"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039829/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fca83d133dfbce94c6d6fb8122c09b1e7028fadefab673818953b0808b76345f"} {"question" "q-81377" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r